{"repositoryId":1261386095,"availability":"available","full":"Syracuse3DPrintingOrg/PantryRaider","name":"PantryRaider","description":"Home Assistant Integration for tracking food spoilage. ","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":7,"forks":4,"created":"2026-06-06T16:04:45Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:57:38Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://syracuse3dprintingorg.github.io/PantryRaider/","topics":[],"demo":"https://demo.pantryraider.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.863Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.863Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.863Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:02:05.863Z","stars":7,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Public beta (0.21). The kitchen side has been in daily use for months. The parts that face other people, the Forager companion, remote access, and the Bandit Cub displays, are younger, so this goes out as a beta because that is what it is. Expect rough edges and occasional breaking changes; back up your data before updating. Upgrading never resets a kitchen that already works. Bug reports are very welcome in the issues tab, and they are the point of a beta.","Your data stays on your hardware; the few optional features that reach the internet are spelled out in the privacy policy.","A self-hosted food tracker that helps you manage what's in your fridge, reduce waste, and plan meals. Built to run entirely on your own hardware with no cloud dependency required."],"features":["AI-powered photo import: photograph a pile of groceries and get them all queued for review at once, without typing anything","Barcode scanning with LLM enrichment: scan barcodes via camera, USB scanner, or manual entry; Open Food Facts provides product data, and an optional LLM pass cleans up messy names and fills in gaps","Stream Deck kiosk: a dedicated kitchen control surface with large buttons for the most common actions, auto-rotation support, and configurable text size; no phone required","Home Assistant integration: a native HACS integration that pairs from the kitchen screen and exposes your food counts, timers, thermometer readings, printer status, and screen controls as entities, with notify entities…","Bandit Cubs: small ESP32 kitchen displays you flash from your browser; they listen to your kitchen's Bluetooth broadcast to show expiring items, running timers, and probe temperatures, and you update one by flashing it…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Syracuse3DPrintingOrg/PantryRaider/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5c230226affb5aef2ee5a01f84396c0671cbf6d4130b241b5315bdf9050e882e","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:06.010Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:02:06.010Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Public beta (0.21). The kitchen side has been in daily use for months. The parts that face other people, the Forager companion, remote access, and the Bandit Cub displays, are younger, so this goes out as a beta because that is what it is. Expect rough edges and occasional breaking changes; back up your data before updating. Upgrading never resets a kitchen that already works. Bug reports are very welcome in the issues tab, and they are the point of a beta.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Syracuse3DPrintingOrg/PantryRaider/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"Two-factor authentication: optional TOTP (app-based 2FA) on top of password login; works offline with any authenticator app","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Syracuse3DPrintingOrg/PantryRaider/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A kitchen screen that signs itself in: the screen on a Pi appliance signs in on its own each time it starts, so a wall panel never waits at the sign-in page","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Syracuse3DPrintingOrg/PantryRaider/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","t